  <text>
    <body>
      <div>
        <head>In the directories</head>
        <p>Mrs A. H. Kopmann, cigar manufacturer, is listed at No. 75 <ref target="civic?id=Madeline%20Street">Madeline Street</ref> from 1910 to 1925. In 1935 Mrs A. H. Kopmann, tobacconist, is at No. 615 <ref target="civic?id=Swanston%20Street">Swanston Street</ref>.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <head>On the electoral roll</head>
        <p>Anna Helene Kopmann, cigar manufacturer, is on the 1919 <ref target="civic?id=Electoral-Rolls">electoral roll</ref> at 75 Madeline Street.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <head>Neighbours</head>
        <p>Solomon Cohen, tailor, is next door at No. 77 from 1910 to 1920, and in 1925 it is the <ref target="civic?id=Queensberry%20hotel">Queensberry hotel</ref>, at Nos 77 to 79. <ref target="civic?id=Lazarus%20Cruchek">Lazarus Cruchek</ref>, furniture dealer, is two doors away at No. 71.</p>
      </div>
